laconic-check calibration corpus

These files are human-written Australian Government prose that
src/seeded_faults.rs lints to measure false findings. They are test data, not
part of the Laconic skills, and neither FSL-1.1-ALv2 nor the MIT License
applies to them.

Each file is based on a Productivity Commission report, copyright
Commonwealth of Australia, licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 3.0
Australia licence (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/au/), as the
copyright page of each report states. The Commission's own copyright page
(https://www.pc.gov.au/copyright/) licenses its copyright work under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence. Both were checked on
2 November 2026. Neither licence covers the Commonwealth Coat of Arms or
content supplied by third parties. These files keep the reports' text and
drop their images, figures, tables and set-off quotations; short quotations
inside the running text remain.

- rising-inequality-2018.md. Source: based on Productivity Commission data,
  Rising inequality? A stocktake of the evidence. Productivity Commission 2018,
  Commission Research Paper, Canberra; released 28 August 2018.
  https://assets.pc.gov.au/research/completed/rising-inequality/rising-inequality.docx
- right-to-repair-2021.md. Source: based on Productivity Commission data,
  Right to Repair. Productivity Commission 2021, Inquiry Report no. 97,
  Canberra; publicly released 1 December 2021.
  https://assets.pc.gov.au/inquiries/completed/repair/report/repair.docx
- vulnerable-supply-chains-2021.md. Source: based on Productivity Commission
  data, Vulnerable Supply Chains, Study Report. Productivity Commission 2021,
  Study Report, July; publicly released 13 August 2021.
  https://assets.pc.gov.au/inquiries/completed/supply-chains/report/supply-chains.docx

Changes: the Word versions above were downloaded on 2 November 2026 and
converted to Markdown with pandoc 3.13:

    pandoc REPORT.docx -t gfm --wrap=none --eol=lf --lua-filter=prose.lua

where prose.lua drops images, figures, tables and block quotes, so the boxes,
data tables and set-off quotations from inquiry participants are omitted:

    function Image() return {} end
    function Figure() return {} end
    function Table() return {} end
    function BlockQuote() return {} end

Trailing spaces were then removed from each line. The text is otherwise as
published, in the Commission's own style.
